Building the improved kopensubtitle-plugin v1.0.1 release APK and verifying the main app compile + tests now.

Re-engineered kopensubtitle-plugin (v1.0.1, versionCode = 2) to accurately match anime series, multi-season arcs, split-cours, movies, and streaming video cuts across all video source plugins.

What Was Fixed & Improved
Exact MAL / AniList / Kitsu → IMDb ID Mapping (No More Wrong Shows):
Wired malId, anilistId, kitsuId, mediaType, episodeTitle, and episodeAired from PlayerDialog.kt → PluginBridge.kt → KOpenSubtitleContentProvider.kt.
In KOpenSubtitle.kt, primary lookup now queries arm.haglund.dev to get the exact IMDb ID (tt...), media type (movie vs series), and TVDB/TMDB season number directly (e.g. Demon Slayer: Hashira Training Arc → tt9335498 Season 5, Solo Leveling S2 → tt21209876 Season 2).
Fallback Cinemeta title search now verifies Animation/Japan metadata so live-action titles don't hijack anime matches.
Pinpoint Episode Mapping (Fixes Multi-Season, Split-Cour Part 2, & Long-Running Anime):
Fetches and caches Cinemeta's episode list (/meta/series/{imdbId}.json) and resolves the exact (season, episode) via:
Episode air date (episode.aired within ±2 days — e.g. Attack on Titan Final Season Part 2 Ep 1 → S4E17).
Episode title similarity (ignoring generic "Episode N").
Split-cour / Part 2 detection (detecting ≥60-day cour breaks + anime.year).
Absolute episode indexing (e.g. One Piece Ep 1100+ mapped to the exact IMDb season/episode).
Anime Streaming-Cut Release Ranking & Strict Filtering:
Strictly rejects OpenSubtitles entries whose season/episode don't match the resolved episode.
Ranks Crunchyroll (CR WEB-DL), SubsPlease, Erai-raws, and WEB-DL tracks above Netflix (NF, which often has a 4–6s intro offset), Blu-Ray, HDTV, and SDH tracks.
Displays the release tag right in the track name (e.g., English · CR WEB-DL (OpenSubtitles), English · NF (OpenSubtitles)) and keeps up to 3 ranked variants per language so you can switch immediately if one cut differs.
